  "description": {
    "text": "Kagemaru Himeno, one of the card game's illustrators, wrote How I Became a Pokémon Card (ポケモンカードになったワケ), a manga in six volumes in which each chapter tells the story behind one of her card illustrations. Each volume came with a card she drew for it, in a paper envelope mounted inside the book: Mankey with volume 1 on 22 May 1999, then Psyduck (September 1999), Jynx (January 2000), Sunkern (August 2000), Hoppip (July 2001) and, with the last volume on 22 September 2001, the birthday Pikachu, \"_____'s Pikachu\".\n\nThe cards print no number. The first five name themselves bonus cards of the Pokémon Card Books along their bottom edge and carry the series' mark, a small card on an open book, in place of a set symbol; the Pikachu has neither. Wizards of the Coast later printed the Psyduck's art in English as Black Star promo 20.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: \"How I became a Pokémon card\" (Natta Wake), a guide to the manga and cards",
        "url": "https://www.elitefourum.com/t/how-i-became-a-pokemon-card-natta-wake-a-guide-to-the-manga-and-cards/42359"
      },
      {
