        "text": "How I Became a Pokémon Card (ポケモンカードになったワケ) is a manga series by Kagemaru Himeno, one of the card game's illustrators, in six volumes from 1999 to 2001. Each chapter tells the story behind one of her card illustrations, and each volume came with a card of her own, in a paper envelope mounted inside the book.\n\nThis card came with volume 6, the last, published on 22 September 2001, whose final chapter, \"Akari and Pikachu's Birthday\", tells its story. Its name leaves a blank for the owner's, its attack is called Birthday, and a box at the bottom has room to write a trainer's name and birthday. It is the only one of the six without the series' card-and-book mark, and its bottom edge says only that it can't be used in official tournaments.",
        "sources": [
          {
            "title": "Elite Fourum: \"How I became a Pokémon card\" (Natta Wake), a guide to the manga and cards",
